id: decisions/019-failure-posture
title: "Unknown means closed; not every question is a gate"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'failure-posture'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: failure-posture
axis_gloss: "what a check does when it cannot decide: it blocks and stops the work, or it records a warning and lets the work continue"
poles:
  a: fail-closed
  b: warn-and-proceed
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 13.7
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(13) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.5)"

question: >
  When a check cannot decide, does the work stop or does it note the doubt and
  go on, and which open questions count as checks?

why_it_matters: >
  Six written rules say a gate that cannot decide stays closed and foregrounded,
  and the tests enforce it; one written rule says an open question blocks only
  when it would change a decision, and the arena document owes revision only
  when a failure recurs, with no counter anywhere. A bot inherits whether an
  unanswered question in questions/ halts its move; a child Yawn inherits
  whether unknown is a stop or a note.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    11 judgments sit at fail-closed (6 authored) and 2 at warn-and-proceed (1
    authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Who may set blocks_action on a new question: its author, a bot, or only Dave.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      Every check fails closed. An unknown, disputed or missing assessment leaves
      the gate closed and foregrounded; every open question is a gate until
      answered.
    cost: "questions/open-questions.yawn loses its need-not-block rule; the repository-rename question (blocks_action: false) becomes a blocker."
    risk: "Delay without safety on questions that cannot change a decision, which is the reason J0543 gives against it."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "tests/orientation-map-v0.1.test.mjs 'machine inference cannot clear any hard gate' and 'typed holds and selector options fail closed' already cover gates; A would add a check that no open question carries blocks_action: false."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0016"
      - "J0228"
      - "J0544"
      - "J0575"
      - "J0603"
      - "J0648"
  - name: B
    description: >
      Checks warn and proceed. A blocker is recorded as state and the move
      continues; a rule is revised when its failure has been seen more than once.
    cost: "Rewriting the negative_assessment_boundary in core/inquiry-selection.yawn and the sender_rule in automation/yawn.bot.pr-notification.yawn; deleting three fail-closed tests."
    risk: "A confident model assessment clears a gate; a notification is routed around an unapproved sender; both are exactly what the authored rules forbid."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "None on this side; B is the absence of the fail-closed tests."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0185"
      - "J0543"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Gates fail closed: unknown, disputed or missing evidence leaves a gate closed
      and foregrounded, and machine inference never clears one. An open question is
      a gate only when it carries blocks_action: true and a why_it_matters; a
      question marked blocks_action: false does not stop movement. Any rule that
      fires on recurrence names the ledger that counts.
    cost: "Two sentences in questions/open-questions.yawn rules; a blocks_action flag on every open question (three of four already carry it); a ledger reference in core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 18."
    risk: "Whoever sets blocks_action decides what can be skipped; if a bot sets it, the carve-out becomes a bypass."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Keep the three fail-closed tests; add to tests/ a check that every entry in questions/open-questions.yawn carries blocks_action and why_it_matters, and that any .yawn using recurrence as a trigger names a ledger path that exists."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0016"
      - "J0228"
      - "J0543"
      - "J0544"
      - "J0603"
      - "J0648"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.85
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Fail-closed has six authored judgments, one proof-attached (J0228, enforced by
    'unknown hard-gate evidence is foregrounded and never rewritten as clear') and
    one outcome-attached (J0603). The only authored warn-and-proceed judgment
    (J0543) is not about gates at all; it is about which questions are gates, and
    J0544 shows the artifacts already implement it with blocks_action flags. The
    two rules do not collide once written together. The one real warn-and-proceed
    is J0185's recurrence threshold with no counter, which C closes by requiring
    the ledger. This is nearly decided already; it needs one paragraph where the
    two rules meet.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "questions/open-questions.yawn rules say a question blocks when and only when blocks_action: true, and every open question carries the flag with a why_it_matters"
    - "core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 18 names the ledger that counts recurrences"
    - "The fail-closed tests in tests/orientation-map-v0.1.test.mjs and tests/inquiry-selection-receipt-v0.1.test.mjs keep passing and a new test checks the blocks_action flag"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A bot proceeds past a question marked blocks_action: true, or a gate assessed
    unknown is rendered clear, and no test fails.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0016"
  - "J0228"
  - "J0544"
  - "J0575"
  - "J0603"
  - "J0648"
  - "J0185"
  - "J0543"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
